    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0881" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to
                        the Greek Govemment-in-Exile in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leeper</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Eden</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d468-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-03">December 3, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi></p>
                <p>I spoke to you yesterday about our desire for a very much closer co-operation
                    with the Americans in the Balkans, both as regards policy and execution of
                    policy. Both Mr. Stevenson<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d468-f2"/> and I are in full agreement on this point, and I cannot
                    do better than attach a copy of a paper he has written on the subject, which is
                    on the Agenda for the Middle East Defence Committee<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d468-f3"/> this morning.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d468-f4"/> I
                    understand that most members of the Defence Committee have already signified in
                    advance their warm approval of these proposals.</p>
                <closer><signed>R. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Leeper</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi>, 3rd December, 1943.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d468-a1.xml" xpointer="d468-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d468-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d468-f1-content">
                <p>This document, which is marked “Copy”, was presumably passed to Roosevelt during the Second Cairo Conference;
                    when and by whom this was done are not indicated.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d468-f2" n="2" xml:id="d468-f2-content">
                <p>Ralph Clarmont Skrine Stevenson, British
                    Ambassador to the Yugoslav Government-in-Exile in Egypt.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d468-f3" n="3" xml:id="d468-f3-content">
                <p>A United Kingdom policy-coordinating agency, functioning at Cairo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d468-f4" n="*" xml:id="d468-f4-content">
                <p>Now approved by M. E. D. C. [Footnote in the
                    source text.]</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
